ITEMS = ((('what should i do if an adult is choking', 'how do i help an adult who is choking during adult choking', 'what is the first aid for choking in adults', 'how to respond when a grown up is choking', 'what to do when an adult cannot breathe from choking', 'how do you help a choking adult', 'what helps an adult choking on food', 'how can i assist an adult who is choking', 'what is the best response to adult choking', 'how should i handle choking in a grown up'), 'If an adult is choking and cannot cough, speak or breathe, encourage them to cough and give firm back blows between the shoulder blades. If the blockage remains, trained responders may use abdominal thrusts. Call emergency services if it does not clear, and get first-aid training to practise these skills.'), (('how do i know if an adult is choking for a choking adult', 'what are the signs of choking in adults', 'how to tell mild from severe choking in adults', 'what does an adult look like when choking', 'can an adult choke and still cough', 'how to recognise choking in a grown up', 'what sounds indicate adult choking', 'how do i know when choking is serious', 'what if a choking adult can still talk', 'how to spot a blocked airway in an adult'), 'An adult who is choking may clutch the throat, be unable to speak or cough, and make a high-pitched sound or no sound at all. If they can cough strongly, encourage coughing and watch closely. Call emergency services if they cannot breathe, speak or cough effectively.'), (('how to give back blows to a choking adult', 'where to hit a choking adult on the back', 'are back blows useful for adult choking', 'how many back blows for an adult in first aid', 'what is the correct back blow technique for adults', 'should i bend a choking adult forward', 'how do i support an adult while giving back blows', 'what if back blows do not help a choking adult', 'can back blows clear adult choking', 'when to use back blows on a choking grown up'), 'Stand behind the choking adult, lean them forward and give firm back blows between the shoulder blades with the heel of your hand. Check after each blow to see if the airway has cleared. If the blockage persists, call emergency services and seek trained help for thrusts.'), (('how do i do abdominal thrusts on an adult', 'what is the abdominal thrust technique for choking adults', 'when are abdominal thrusts used for adults', 'should i give abdominal thrusts to a choking adult', 'how to perform the heimlich manoeuvre on adults', 'is it safe to do abdominal thrusts on a grown up during adult choking', 'what if abdominal thrusts do not clear choking', 'where do i press for abdominal thrusts during adult choking', 'can abdominal thrusts hurt a choking adult', 'who should learn abdominal thrusts for adults'), 'Abdominal thrusts may be used when back blows have not cleared severe choking in an adult. They involve firm inward and upward pressure just above the navel, and can cause bruising. Learn the technique on a proper course, and call emergency services if the blockage does not clear.'), (('what if a choking adult becomes unconscious', 'how to handle an unconscious choking adult', 'should i start cpr for a choking adult', 'what to do when a choking grown up collapses', 'how to place an unconscious choking adult', 'what if the adult stops responding while choking', 'how to check the mouth of an unconscious choking adult', 'what happens if choking leads to unconsciousness', 'should i call emergency services for an unconscious choking adult', 'how to help a collapsed adult after choking'), 'If a choking adult becomes unconscious, call emergency services and begin CPR, with rescue breaths if you are trained. Do not blind sweep the mouth with your fingers. Ask a qualified person to take over as soon as possible and follow their instructions.'), (('what to do if an adult chokes on food during adult choking', 'how to help an adult choking during a meal', 'what if a piece of food blocks an adult airway', 'how to clear food choking in adults', 'should i give water to an adult choking on food', 'what is the response to food choking in a grown up', 'can a drink help adult choking on food', 'how to deal with a blocked airway after eating during adult choking', 'when to call help if an adult chokes on food', 'what not to do when food causes adult choking'), 'Do not give water or food to an adult choking on food, as it can worsen the blockage. Encourage coughing if they can, and use back blows if they cannot breathe or speak. Call emergency services if the food does not come out quickly.'), (('what to do if i am choking alone as an adult', 'how can an adult help themselves when choking', 'is there self help for adult choking', 'how to treat choking on myself', 'what can i do alone if my airway is blocked during adult choking', 'can i give myself abdominal thrusts during adult choking', 'how to call for help while choking alone', 'what to lean on when choking by myself', 'is self treatment safe for adult choking', 'how should an adult cope with choking alone'), 'If you are choking alone, call emergency services straight away and make noise to attract help. You may press your upper abdomen against a firm edge to try to dislodge the object. Get medical help afterwards because an airway blockage can cause hidden injury.'), (('how to help a pregnant adult who is choking', 'are chest thrusts used for choking in pregnancy', 'what if an adult cannot have abdominal thrusts', 'how to help a larger adult who is choking', 'is choking care different for pregnant adults', 'what to do if abdominal thrusts are not suitable during adult choking', 'how to assist a choking adult with a disability', 'what if i cannot wrap my arms around a choking adult', 'how to adapt first aid for adult choking', 'when to get urgent help for choking in pregnancy'), 'For a pregnant adult or someone where abdominal thrusts are unsuitable, chest thrusts may be used by a trained responder. Give back blows first and call emergency services if the airway stays blocked. Ask the person what position helps them and get qualified help quickly.'), (('should i see a doctor after choking as an adult', 'what to check after an adult choking episode', 'can choking cause injury in adults', 'do i need medical help after clearing choking', 'what symptoms after adult choking need review', 'how to feel after a choking incident', 'should an older adult be checked after choking', 'what if breathing is noisy after choking', 'when to get checked following adult choking', 'what complications can follow choking in adults'), 'After a choking episode, an adult should be checked by a doctor if breathing remains noisy, there is chest pain, or swallowing is difficult. A forceful thrust can also cause internal injury. Call emergency services if symptoms worsen or breathing becomes difficult again.'), (('when should i call an ambulance for adult choking', 'how long do i wait before calling for choking help', 'is choking in an adult always an emergency', 'what if choking will not clear in an adult', 'should i call emergency services for mild choking', 'when to escalate adult choking', 'what if a choking adult turns blue', 'how urgent is choking in a grown up', 'should i call if a choking adult can still cough', 'what to tell the operator about adult choking'), 'Call emergency services whenever an adult cannot breathe, speak or cough, or if choking does not clear quickly. Tell the operator that it is a blocked airway and follow their guidance. Stay with the person and be ready to give back blows or start CPR.'))
